      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 Wiley-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim.",
        "AbstractText": "The first enantioselective total synthesis of natural dicerandrol\u2005C (1\u2009c) as its enantiomer containing a dimeric tetrahydroxanthenone skeleton is described starting from the enantiopure chromane 6 which was obtained through a Wacker-type cyclization with >99\u2009%\u2009ee. For the formation of the dimeric skeleton a palladium-catalyzed Suzuki reaction was used. The synthesis allowed the confirmation of the absolute configuration of the dicerandrols."
      },
